From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: TabNavigation modes; Tab leaves the island to its host

Tab order now follows the containers: TabIndex orders the children of each container, a container's TabNavigation Once makes it one stop (the focused element inside, else its first) and Cycle keeps Tab going round inside it. Tab past the island's last stop, or Shift+Tab before its first, now hands the focus to the host: DesktopWindowXamlSource.TakeFocusRequested is raised (reason First or Last) when the host listens, else the next tab stop of the host window takes the focus, as in a dialog; only when neither is there does Tab go round the island. DesktopWindowXamlSource.NavigateFocus (it was a stub) brings the focus back to the first or last stop, and XamlSourceFocusNavigationRequest/Result can be made. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
